Subject: [PATCH] new rpg: the Dark Iron Legacy quests keep their quest log slot

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

mod-overseer#1444. NewRpgBaseAction::OrganizeQuestLog runs at the start of
SearchQuestGiverAndAcceptOrReward for a bot in the New RPG state, and does
nothing while the log has two free slots. With fewer, it removes in turn:

  1. every quest IsQuestCapableDoing refuses (Quest::GetType() != 0, a
     dungeon-type quest) or IsQuestWorthDoing refuses, or that has failed;
  2. every quest of another zone than the bot stands in;
  3. if that freed fewer than 8, every quest left in the log.

Dark Iron Legacy (3801, 3802) is a dungeon-type quest (QuestInfoID 81) in the
Blackrock Depths zone (1584), so the first two passes always take it, and
the family's logs sit at 18 to 23 of 25 slots. Measured on the dev realm,
2026-11-08: the ghost detour (#1422) took 3801 and 3802 for Zug, Oz and Zrog
at 09:30 UTC; by 16:30 UTC 3801 was rewarded for all three, 3802 was in nobody's
log, and no character on the realm held any dungeon-type quest in progress.
Zug's run then killed Fineous Darkvire with no 3802, so Ironfel could not drop
and the family still had no Shadowforge Key.

WHAT IT CHANGES

OrganizeQuestLog skips 3801 and 3802 in all three passes. Every other quest is
removed exactly as before, and the quest still obeys every other rule (a
completed 3802 is turned in; an abandoned one is abandoned by whoever asks).

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream leaving dungeon-type quests a bot already holds alone when it tidies
its log, or the family leaving the New RPG state for good.

APPLIES TO

    mod-playerbots @ 40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130
    src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp, OrganizeQuestLog
    Replayed by tests/replay_legacy_quest_log.py against the pinned file
    (tests/fixtures/legacy_quest_log/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp).

diff --git a/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp b/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp
index ba23668..baddd2a 100644
--- a/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/World/Rpg/Action/NewRpgBaseAction.cpp
@@ -595,6 +595,15 @@ bool NewRpgBaseAction::IsQuestCapableDoing(Quest const* quest)
     return true;
 }
 
+// The Dark Iron Legacy chain (3801, 3802) is how a family earns the Shadowforge
+// Key. Both are dungeon-type quests in the Blackrock Depths zone, so the three
+// passes below read them as "not capable" and "other zone" and removed them at
+// the first tidy of a nearly full log (mod-overseer#1444).
+static bool KeepsItsLogSlot(uint32 questId)
+{
+    return questId == 3801 || questId == 3802;
+}
+
 bool NewRpgBaseAction::OrganizeQuestLog()
 {
     int32 freeSlotNum = 0;
@@ -618,6 +627,9 @@ bool NewRpgBaseAction::OrganizeQuestLog()
         if (!questId)
             continue;
 
+        if (KeepsItsLogSlot(questId))
+            continue;
+
         Quest const* quest = sObjectMgr->GetQuestTemplate(questId);
         if (!IsQuestWorthDoing(quest) || !IsQuestCapableDoing(quest) ||
             bot->GetQuestStatus(questId) == QUEST_STATUS_FAILED)
@@ -649,6 +661,9 @@ bool NewRpgBaseAction::OrganizeQuestLog()
         if (!questId)
             continue;
 
+        if (KeepsItsLogSlot(questId))
+            continue;
+
         Quest const* quest = sObjectMgr->GetQuestTemplate(questId);
         const int64_t botZoneId = this->bot->GetZoneId();
 
@@ -680,6 +695,9 @@ bool NewRpgBaseAction::OrganizeQuestLog()
         if (!questId)
             continue;
 
+        if (KeepsItsLogSlot(questId))
+            continue;
+
         Quest const* quest = sObjectMgr->GetQuestTemplate(questId);
         LOG_DEBUG("playerbots", "[New RPG] {} drop quest {}", bot->GetName(), questId);
         WorldPacket packet(CMSG_QUESTLOG_REMOVE_QUEST);
